Rights in the names and marks UU Remote, NetEase, and related designations,
and in the official software, documentation, assets, and services, are held
by NetEase and other respective rightsholders as provided by law. These names
are referenced to identify the compatibility target and research sources,
not to claim ownership of those rights.

This project claims neither original authorship nor exclusive licensing
rights over the UU Remote protocol itself, interface facts needed for
interoperability, field meanings, or behavioral rules. No copyright
reservation is asserted over ideas, processes, methods of operation,
mathematical concepts, or other subject matter excluded from copyright
protection by applicable law. Rights in specific code or documentation
expression, trademarks, patents, trade secrets, and other subject matter
must be assessed separately.

Copyright (c) 2026 djkcyl and the respective contributors, solely in their
original contributions to the extent they lawfully hold the relevant rights.
This attribution does not cover third-party works or assert ownership of all
intellectual property in the repository or program as a whole. The absence
of a copyright header does not establish that a file is original to this project.

Porting, translating, or rewriting an existing implementation in Rust does
not automatically confer exclusive rights over the original work or remove
its license obligations. The scope and licensing of third-party code,
derivative code, and related modifications depend on their actual sources,
original licenses, and applicable law, not merely on file locations or
